{
  "id": "L-008",
  "title": "Infinite Limits and Vertical Asymptotes",
  "atom_ids": ["A-08"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The outputs can also diverge: as "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "x" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " approaches a point, the values of "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "f(x)" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " may grow without bound. The notation "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\lim_{x \\to a} f(x) = \\infty" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " names this behaviour — it is not a claim that a limit exists as a number. A limit is a real number; "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\infty" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " is a report of unbounded growth."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "definition",
      "term": "Vertical asymptote",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The line "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "x = a" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " is a vertical asymptote of "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "f" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " when at least one one-sided limit of "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "f" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " at "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "a" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " is "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\infty" },
        { "type": "text", "text": " or " },
        { "type": "math", "source": "-\\infty" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " — the values diverge as "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "x" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " approaches "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "a" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " from one side."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Infinite limits are decided by sign. To analyse "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "f" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " near "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "a" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", ask what sign each factor has just to the left of "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "a" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and just to the right."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "title": "Signs decide the side",
      "problem": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Find the one-sided limits "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\lim_{x \\to 3^-} \\dfrac{2x}{x - 3}" },
        { "type": "text", "text": " and " },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\lim_{x \\to 3^+} \\dfrac{2x}{x - 3}" },
        { "type": "text", "text": "." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Near "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "x = 3" },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " the numerator "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "2x" },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is about 6, positive on both sides."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "For "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "x" },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " just below 3, the denominator "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "x - 3" },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is negative and tiny, so the quotient is a large negative number: "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "\\lim_{x \\to 3^-} \\dfrac{2x}{x - 3} = -\\infty" },
          { "type": "text", "text": "." }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "For "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "x" },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " just above 3, the denominator is positive and tiny, so the quotient is large and positive: "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "\\lim_{x \\to 3^+} \\dfrac{2x}{x - 3} = \\infty" },
          { "type": "text", "text": "." }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The one-sided limits disagree — both diverge, but in opposite directions — so by the existence test in L-002 the two-sided limit does not exist. The line "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "x = 3" },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is a vertical asymptote."
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "src": "figures/vertical-asymptote.png",
      "atom_id": "A-08",
      "caption": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "For "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "y = \\dfrac{1}{x - 2}" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " the curve drops to "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "-\\infty" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " as "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "x \\to 2^-" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and rises to "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\infty" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " as "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "x \\to 2^+" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". The dashed line "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "x = 2" },
        { "type": "text", "text": " is a vertical asymptote." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "widget",
      "name": "plot",
      "version": "1.0",
      "parameters": {
        "series": [
          {
            "label": "left of 2: y = 1/(x - 2)",
            "points": [
              [0.3, -0.588], [0.6, -0.714], [1.0, -1.0], [1.4, -1.667],
              [1.7, -3.333], [1.85, -6.667], [1.95, -20.0]
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "right of 2: y = 1/(x - 2)",
            "points": [
              [2.1, 10.0], [2.2, 5.0], [2.5, 2.0], [3.0, 1.0],
              [4.0, 0.5], [5.0, 0.333], [6.0, 0.25]
            ]
          }
        ],
        "xlabel": "x",
        "ylabel": "y",
        "title": "1/(x - 2): unbounded growth on both sides of x = 2"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "warning",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Writing "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\lim_{x \\to a} f(x) = \\infty" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " is shorthand for the values growing without bound. The limit does not exist as a number, and the function is undefined at "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "a" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " — no output is ever 'equal to infinity'."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "formative",
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Explain why "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\lim_{x \\to 2} \\dfrac{1}{x - 2}" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " does not exist, even though both one-sided limits exist as "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\infty" },
        { "type": "text", "text": " and " },
        { "type": "math", "source": "-\\infty" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". Use the one-sided existence test from L-002."
        }
      ],
      "kind": "free_response"
    }
  ]
}